  "type": "Exercise",
  "number": "4.13.2",
  "title": "Tabletop RPG Party Roster &amp; Encumbrance Audit.",
  "body": " Tabletop RPG Party Roster & Encumbrance Audit   In Chapter 3, you calculated ability modifiers and evaluated feat qualifications for an individual character. When managing a gaming campaign, a game master must evaluate an entire adventuring party to calculate group encumbrance, identify party extremes, and determine average resilience.  Write a program that audits an adventuring party by reading character records from a text file named party_roster.txt or through an interactive sentinel loop.   Data Format ( party_roster.txt ): Each character record occupies four consecutive lines:  Character name ( String )  Character class ( String )  Strength score ( int , 3 to 20)  Constitution score ( int , 3 to 20)     Program Requirements:    File Input: Open and read party_roster.txt using while (fileScanner.hasNext()) . Use nextLine() for names and classes, and parse the scores. Guard the newline transition using the pattern from .    Processing: For each character, compute their Strength modifier using integer division ( ), their carrying capacity ( ), and their starting hit points ( , where Fighter = 12, Paladin\/Cleric = 10, Rogue = 8, Wizard = 6).    Variable Roles:   Stepper: Count the total party members ( partySize ).  Gatherer: Accumulate total party carrying capacity ( totalCapacity ).  Most-Wanted Holders: Track both the strongest hero ( maxStrength , strongestName ) and the character with the lowest hit points ( minHp , mostVulnerableName ).     One-Way Flag: A boolean flag ( hasHeavyLifter ) that starts false and flips to true if any single character has a Strength score of 18 or higher.    Output: Display a formatted roster table on the console with right-aligned numbers and left-aligned names, followed by party statistics.      Testing Requirement: Design a test plan verifying:  An empty roster file (zero iterations).  A single-character party.  A party with negative and positive ability modifiers.  Tied attribute scores.    Here is an example of the program running:   PARTY ROSTER AUDIT (party_roster.txt) ---------------------------------------------------------------------- NAME CLASS STR (MOD) CARRY CAP HIT POINTS ---------------------------------------------------------------------- Garrett Rogue 14 (+2) 210 lbs 11 Valeria Paladin 18 (+4) 270 lbs 14 Bram Fighter 16 (+3) 240 lbs 13 Elira Wizard 8 (-1) 120 lbs 9 ---------------------------------------------------------------------- Total Party Members : 4 Combined Carrying Cap : 840 lbs Average Party Health : 11.75 HP Strongest Adventurer : Valeria (Strength 18) Most Vulnerable : Elira (9 HP) Heavy Lifter Present? : Yes    "
