  "body": " Terminology: Parameters vs. Arguments  You might hear experienced programmers use the words parameter and argument interchangeably. Technically, the variables declared in the method header are formal parameters , and the expressions passed in the method call are either actual parameters or arguments . In the interest of correctness and clarity, we use the terms parameter or parameter variable for the variables declared within the method header and argument for the expressions passed to the method call.  "
