  "title": "Exoplanet Orbital Period and Habitable Zone Model.",
  "body": " Exoplanet Orbital Period and Habitable Zone Model   Astronomers discovering extrasolar planets use physical laws to characterize planetary orbits. By Kepler's Third Law, a planet's orbital period (in Earth years) around a host star of mass (in solar masses ) at semi-major axis (in Astronomical Units, AU) is: A star's circumstellar habitable zone (the range of orbital distances where liquid water can exist) scales with the star's bolometric luminosity (relative to our Sun):   Design and implement two collaborating classes: Star and Exoplanet .   UML Class Diagram for Star     Star     - name : String  - massSolarMasses : double  - luminositySolar : double      + Star(name : String, massSolarMasses : double, luminositySolar : double)  + getName() : String  + getMassSolarMasses() : double  + getLuminositySolar() : double  + getHabitableZoneInnerAU() : double  + getHabitableZoneOuterAU() : double  + isInHabitableZone(orbitalDistanceAU : double) : boolean  + toString() : String       UML Class Diagram for Exoplanet     Exoplanet     - designation : String  - semiMajorAxisAU : double  - hostStar : Star      + Exoplanet(designation : String, semiMajorAxisAU : double, hostStar : Star)  + getDesignation() : String  + getSemiMajorAxisAU() : double  + getHostStar() : Star  + calculateOrbitalPeriodYears() : double  + calculateOrbitalPeriodDays() : double  + isPotentiallyHabitable() : boolean  + toString() : String      Class Invariants and Requirements:   name and designation must not be null or blank.  massSolarMasses > 0.0 and luminositySolar > 0.0 .  semiMajorAxisAU > 0.0 and hostStar != null .    Exoplanet.isPotentiallyHabitable() delegates directly to hostStar.isInHabitableZone(this.semiMajorAxisAU) , demonstrating message passing.    Write an automated test suite in ExoplanetTest modeling our Sun ( ) and Earth ( ), verifying that Earth has an orbital period of approximately 365.25 days and resides within the habitable zone. Then test Proxima Centauri and Proxima b.    Convert years to days using periodYears * 365.25 .   "
