  "title": "Aviation Flight Category and Crosswind Safety Advisor.",
  "body": " Aviation Flight Category and Crosswind Safety Advisor   General aviation pilots rely on METAR weather observations to determine whether flight conditions meet FAA flight rules: Visual Flight Rules (VFR), Marginal VFR (MVFR), or Instrument Flight Rules (IFR). In addition, pilots must calculate the crosswind component relative to the active runway heading:   Design and implement two classes: an immutable WeatherObservation and an analytical FlightSafetyAdvisor .   UML Class Diagram for WeatherObservation     WeatherObservation     - stationId : String  - visibilityMiles : double  - cloudCeilingFeet : int  - windSpeedKnots : double  - windDirectionDegrees : int      + WeatherObservation(stationId : String, visibilityMiles : double, cloudCeilingFeet : int, windSpeedKnots : double, windDirectionDegrees : int)  + getStationId() : String  + getVisibilityMiles() : double  + getCloudCeilingFeet() : int  + getWindSpeedKnots() : double  + getWindDirectionDegrees() : int  + determineFlightCategory() : String  + toString() : String       UML Class Diagram for FlightSafetyAdvisor     FlightSafetyAdvisor     - maxDemonstratedCrosswindKnots : double      + FlightSafetyAdvisor(maxDemonstratedCrosswindKnots : double)  + getMaxDemonstratedCrosswindKnots() : double  + calculateCrosswindComponent(obs : WeatherObservation, runwayHeadingDegrees : int) : double  + isSafeToLand(obs : WeatherObservation, runwayHeadingDegrees : int) : boolean  + toString() : String      FAA Category Rules and Class Invariants:   visibilityMiles >= 0.0 and cloudCeilingFeet >= 0 .  windSpeedKnots >= 0.0 and windDirectionDegrees between 0 and 360.    determineFlightCategory() returns:   \"VFR\" if ceiling >= 3000 ft and visibility >= 5.0 miles.  \"MVFR\" if ceiling is 1000–2999 ft or visibility is 3.0–4.9 miles.  \"IFR\" if ceiling is < 1000 ft or visibility is < 3.0 miles.      isSafeToLand() returns true if and only if the flight category is \"VFR\" and the crosswind component does not exceed maxDemonstratedCrosswindKnots .    Write unit tests in FlightSafetyTest verifying correct flight category classification and crosswind math across multiple runway headings.   "
