{
  "id": "project-storm-tracker",
  "level": "2",
  "url": "sec-6-12-exercises.html#project-storm-tracker",
  "type": "Exercise",
  "number": "6.13.8",
  "title": "Tropical Cyclone Lifecycle and Saffir-Simpson Tracker.",
  "body": " Tropical Cyclone Lifecycle and Saffir-Simpson Tracker   Meteorological organizations track the lifecycle of tropical cyclones as they intensify and weaken over the ocean. As new aircraft reconnaissance advisories arrive, the system must update the storm's current sustained wind speed, update peak lifetime intensity, and classify the storm on the Saffir-Simpson Hurricane Wind Scale:   Tropical Depression: < 34 knots  Tropical Storm: 34–63 knots  Category 1 Hurricane: 64–82 knots  Category 2 Hurricane: 83–95 knots  Category 3 Major Hurricane: 96–112 knots  Category 4 Major Hurricane: 113–136 knots  Category 5 Major Hurricane: >= 137 knots   Design and implement a stateful tracker class named StormTracker .   UML Class Diagram for StormTracker     StormTracker     - stormName : String  - basin : String  - currentWindSpeedKnots : double  - peakWindSpeedKnots : double  - advisoryCount : int  - active : boolean      + StormTracker(stormName : String, basin : String, initialWindSpeedKnots : double)  + getStormName() : String  + getBasin() : String  + getCurrentWindSpeedKnots() : double  + getPeakWindSpeedKnots() : double  + getAdvisoryCount() : int  + isActive() : boolean  + recordAdvisory(newWindSpeedKnots : double) : void  + markDissipated() : void  + getSaffirSimpsonCategory() : String  + isMajorHurricane() : boolean  + toString() : String      Class Invariants and Requirements:   stormName and basin must not be null or blank.  currentWindSpeedKnots >= 0.0 .  peakWindSpeedKnots >= currentWindSpeedKnots at all times.  advisoryCount >= 1 .    recordAdvisory(newWindSpeedKnots) asserts that the storm isActive() and that newWindSpeedKnots >= 0.0 . It updates currentWindSpeedKnots , increments advisoryCount , and updates peakWindSpeedKnots if the new wind speed exceeds the previous peak.     markDissipated() transitions active to false . Subsequent calls to recordAdvisory() must fail with an assertion error.    Write an automated test class in StormTrackerTest verifying a simulated lifecycle: formation at 30 knots, rapid intensification to a 120-knot Category 4 hurricane, weakening to 50 knots (confirming that peak intensity remains 120 knots), dissipation, and rejection of post-dissipation advisory updates.   "
}
